  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Space Exploration Technologies obligated $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Space Exploration Technologies received 80 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $35.6M, and obligations are down 5.0% year over year. Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $2.2B, followed by National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $684M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation is the largest market by obligations at $1.6B, with Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $519M and Satellite Telecommunications at $474M. Fiscal-year trends show obligations rising from $1.5B in FY21 to a peak of $3.4B in FY24, then moving to $3B in FY25 and $2.8B in FY26. The mix of industries and the concentration in a few large contracts make current-year totals partial, since FY2026 is a fiscal year to date snapshot. This profile highlights where federal dollars are concentrated and which agencies and NAICS markets are driving Space Exploration Technologies’s federal revenue so far this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Space Exploration Technologies’s biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "Department of Defense obligated $2.2B to Space Exploration Technologies in FY2026 to date. National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $684M. Smaller buyers include Department of State at $3.2M and Department of Homeland Security at $1.5M, with other agencies showing nominal or negative obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What federal markets generate Space Exploration Technologies’s obligations?",
        "body": "Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation generated $1.6B in obligations for Space Exploration Technologies in FY2026 to date. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing generated $519M, and Satellite Telecommunications generated $474M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences generated $250M, with remaining markets at much smaller levels."
      }
    ]
  },
