      "q": "How much does Space Exploration Technologies make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Space Exploration Technologies has federal contract obligations of $2.8B in FY2026 to date. Space Exploration Technologies received 80 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $35.6M, and obligations are down 5.0% year over year. Fiscal obligations climbed from $1.5B in FY21 to $3.4B in FY24, then moved to $3B in FY25 and $2.8B in FY26."
